# Event Flow Diagram

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Source as Event Source
    participant Engine as Event Engine
    participant Pipeline as Pipeline
    participant Stages as Pipeline Stages
    participant Bus as Event Bus
    participant Output as Output/Clients

    Source->>Engine: Publish Event
    Engine->>Engine: Create Context
    Engine->>Pipeline: Execute Pipeline

    Pipeline->>Stages: Validation Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: Enrichment Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: Persistence Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: History Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: Broadcast Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: Dispatch Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: AI Stage
    Pipeline->>Stages: Plugin Stage

    alt All Stages Success
        Pipeline-->>Engine: PipelineResult(success=True)
        Engine-->>Source: EventResult(success=True)
    else Some Stages Failed
        Pipeline-->>Engine: PipelineResult(success=False)
        Engine-->>Source: EventResult(errors=[...])
    end

    Pipeline->>Bus: Notify Subscribers
    Bus->>Output: WebSocket Broadcast
    Bus->>Output: Push to Clients

    Note over Pipeline,Output: All stages continue even if one fails
```

## Error Handling Flow

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Stage["Pipeline Stage"]
        Execute[execute()]
        Check[can_execute()?]
        Do[Do Work]
        Catch[catch Exception]
        Fail[Add Error to Result]
        Continue{recoverable?}
    end

    Execute --> Check
    Check -->|Yes| Do
    Check -->|No| Skip[Skip - add warning]
    Skip --> Done[Return Result]

    Do --> Catch
    Catch --> Fail
    Fail --> Continue
    Continue -->|Yes| Done
    Continue -->|No| Cancel[Set cancelled=True]
    Cancel --> Done
```
